# A map built inside the loop and read there, so it is garbage the moment the
# iteration ends. Its sorted view is malloc'd rather than arena-allocated —
# that is what stops a below-mark header ever holding a pointer a rewind can
# free — and the price was that nothing owned it: one view allocated per
# iteration and none freed, unbounded in the iteration count.
#
# Three counters below say it, and bytes_peak says it best: twenty thousand
# views are allocated and eighty bytes are ever held at once, which is one.
# view_allocs and view_frees must stay equal, and the peak must not grow with
# the iteration count — a peak that does is the definition of the leak.
#
# A header born inside the beat dies at the rewind, and that is the only moment
# anything can know its view became garbage.
seed = { "a":0 }

fn tally 0 acc
  print acc

fn tally n acc
  m = put seed "b" n
  tally (n - 1) (acc + length m)

pub play = tally 20000 0
